WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.049
Speaker 1: We have a blockbuster new report
out of Rolling Stone.

00:00:06.049 --> 00:00:11.469
Donald Trump's lawyers increasingly believe
that Mark Meadows, his own former chief of

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:13.589
staff, is going down legally.

00:00:13.589 --> 00:00:18.140
And it seems as though they may be getting
closer and closer to abandoning meadows.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:24.580
Now, there is a parallel story here to this,
which is that yesterday I played for you video

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:32.270
from the January six committee wherein Liz
Cheney says We are now aware of Donald Trump

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:39.640
personally calling a forthcoming witness someone
who has not yet testified and trying to tamper

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:46.260
with the witness, trying to influence or in
some way affect their potentially forthcoming

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:47.260
testimony.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:52.280
We don't know who that person is, but there's
rampant speculation that it's Mark Meadows.

00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:58.410
And parallel to that, there is now this incredible
story from from Rolling Stone that Trump's

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.380
lawyers think Meadows is going down.

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:06.289
And the question now is how to minimize the
sort of secondary damage, the shrapnel with

00:01:06.289 --> 00:01:10.670
which others may be hit if indeed Mark Meadows
testifies and goes down.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:14.439
Rolling Stone Writing Exclusive Trump's lawyers
think Mark Meadows is going down.

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:19.189
The January six committee is probing the former
chief of staff's finances, Rolling Stone has

00:01:19.189 --> 00:01:23.820
learned, adding to a long list of legal headaches.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:27.270
As she opened the January six committee on
Tuesday, Liz Cheney ticked through a list

00:01:27.270 --> 00:01:28.810
of names of people.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:34.170
Trump's legal team have attempted to pin the
blame for the Capitol attack, naming the president's

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.319
lawyers, MAGA friendly lawmakers and others.

00:01:36.319 --> 00:01:42.619
Mark Meadows didn't make the list yet, but
Trump's inner circle increasingly views Meadows

00:01:42.619 --> 00:01:47.850
as a likely fall guy for the former president's
attempts to overturn the 2020 election.

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:52.479
Members of Trump's legal team are actively
planning certain strategies around Meadows

00:01:52.479 --> 00:01:55.829
downfall, including possible criminal charges.

00:01:55.829 --> 00:02:00.869
Trump has himself begun the process of distancing
from some of his one time senior aides alleged

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:03.509
actions around January six.

00:02:03.509 --> 00:02:05.159
This is the new part.

00:02:05.159 --> 00:02:08.959
MEADOWS Already bleak legal prospects could
get even worse because Rolling Stone has learned

00:02:08.959 --> 00:02:13.590
that the January six committee has been quietly
probing his financial dealings and any new

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:20.030
revelations would add to an already long list
of unethical and potentially illegal actions

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:23.519
he's accused of taking on behalf of Donald
Trump.

00:02:23.519 --> 00:02:28.200
Quote, Everyone is strategizing around the
likelihood that Mark is in a lot of trouble,

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.959
says a lawyer close to the former president.

00:02:30.959 --> 00:02:33.290
Everyone who knows what they're doing anyway.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:38.790
Rolling Stone spoke to eight sources familiar
with the matter everyone still in Trump's

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:43.860
orbit or on his legal defense or in Republican
circles in contact with Trump.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:48.450
Everybody's speaking candidly because they
were provided anonymity.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:51.420
So there's a few interesting components to
this.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:57.769
First of all, it would not be unlike Donald
Trump to run a multi-pronged strategy publicly

00:02:57.769 --> 00:03:03.879
distance from the people that might be going
down and privately try to influence them in

00:03:03.879 --> 00:03:06.080
order for them to damage you less.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.530
And it's completely speculative.

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:14.349
But there's the question was the phone call
that Trump made to try to tamper with a witness

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:15.989
to Mark Meadows?

00:03:15.989 --> 00:03:22.969
The other part of this is that Meadows is
actually the financial questions around Meadows,

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:26.329
and the voting questions have been going on
for a while, if I recall correctly.

00:03:26.329 --> 00:03:31.540
There's sort of two avenues to this, and it's
sort of strange that everybody around Trump

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.079
has these problems.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:38.319
Mark Meadows had one issue related to voter
registration.

00:03:38.319 --> 00:03:44.749
I'm kind of giving you the 30,000 foot view,
but apparently Meadows owns a trailer somewhere

00:03:44.749 --> 00:03:50.830
that he has never even been to and was registered
to vote at that address, which is weird, and

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.510
also registered to vote elsewhere.

00:03:52.510 --> 00:03:56.030
So that was one thing we talked about maybe
six, eight, nine months ago, something like

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.030
that.

00:03:57.030 --> 00:04:01.610
And then again, if I'm going from memory,
I believe that on the financial side, there's

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:07.329
something tax related to Mark Meadows and
it also may relate to what state do you formally

00:04:07.329 --> 00:04:09.599
live in or whatever the case may be.

00:04:09.599 --> 00:04:13.939
So if and how that connects directly to Trump
is a question, but anything that puts him

00:04:13.939 --> 00:04:18.710
more on the radar of investigators is potentially
bad for Donald Trump.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:23.800
So as far as the witnesses, there's a January
6th hearing sometime next week.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:24.800
I don't.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:26.600
Even know that it's been scheduled specifically
yet.

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:30.630
And we don't know who the witness is going
to be, who the witnesses potentially are going

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:31.630
to be.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:34.650
We've been told it's going to be absolutely
stunning.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.730
Could it be Meadows?

00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:38.140
Could it be Steve Bannon?

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:39.500
I don't know.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:43.640
But it could be maybe the most interesting
day of the hearings altogether.

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:51.270
Liz Cheney made clear this is a witness you
have not yet seen and that there's a long

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:54.350
list of people that could fall into that category.

00:04:54.350 --> 00:04:55.790
But we will soon know.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:05:03.690
And if Meadows goes down, I mean, remember
the strategy from these people, Trump, etc.,

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:08.120
has been, whenever anyone gets in trouble,
minimize their role, minimize their role in

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:12.200
the Trump campaign or the administration or
in whatever.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:19.010
It's going to be impossible to minimize the
role of the last and final chief of staff

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:24.500
that Donald Trump had, who was personally
doing the bidding of Trump in the lead up

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:25.850
to the January six riot.

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:26.850
I mean, they'll try.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:27.850
Of course they'll try.

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:33.360
But it's not going to be I think even the
average American, as we like to say, is going

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:34.930
to see through that.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:35.930
Let me know your thoughts.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:39.360
Who do you expect to be the blockbuster witness
coming up next week?

00:05:39.360 --> 00:06:04.760
You can find me on Twitter at David Pakman.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:56.250
And we'll be covering it, of course

